Z||000000||Hank is Here||11-27-2000||12:48 PM||||I had the dew wipes on another car get really bad on my with lots of cracks, that car had steel doors.  Needless to say the doors are rusting out from the inside. For a quick fix to keep water from getting inside I took "Shoe Goo" and applied over cracks in the wipes.  This make the wipes water tight once again, there can still be dirt trapped in the wipe to scratch the window so this is not a total fix.  You can easily tell the shoe goo is on the wips, but it is watertight, and the shoe good firms up well.<P>Mark Johnson ||||reg||1
